# One branch per request

Each new feature or bug the user asks for gets its own branch. Start it from the latest `origin/main`. Do not add that work to `main`, to an open pull request, or to a branch that already belongs to a different request.

- A feature uses `feature/short-topic`.
- A bug uses `fix/short-topic`.

```powershell
git fetch origin
git checkout -b feature/double-unders origin/main
```

A follow-up that continues the same request stays on that branch. A new request starts a new branch, even when the current branch is clean. Open a pull request only when the user asks.
